/**
 * Regular expressions with the syntax and the semantics of RE2, written in TorbScript: [Regex] compiles a pattern once,
 * and matching runs in time linear in the length of the text - there is no backtracking, so there are no backreferences
 * and no lookaround, and no pattern can take a program down with a text it was handed. The engine is the same code in
 * the VM and in a native binary, so both answer the same.
 *
 *     const pattern = Regex.tryFrom(raw"(?P<key>\w+)=(?P<value>\w+)")?
 *     for found in pattern.findAll("a=1 b=2") {
 *       print "{found.named("key")} is {found.named("value")}"
 *     }
 *
 * A pattern works on characters, and every position it answers is a byte offset into the text, as every position of a
 * `String` is. Named groups decode into a type through `Decode` ([RegexMatch.decoded]).
 */

public use Regex, RegexMatch, GroupRange from "./regex"
public use RegexError from "./syntax"
